From ddcac270514da5d8af607b323e107012706fde5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:24:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] .14 Risk Gate: required-vs-optional symbol handling for
 full coin universe

Extends the same required-vs-optional pattern already shipped in .12/.13:
REQUIRED_SYMBOLS (BTC/ETH) remain the only symbols whose absence, mutual
timestamp desynchronization, or candidate-consistency failure can block
the whole risk-gate decision. Every other symbol .13 now reports (the
full discovered coin universe) is evaluated and risk-gated independently.

Specific changes:
- verify_symbol_set() / verify_timestamp_synchronization() explicitly
  scoped to REQUIRED_SYMBOLS only (timestamp sync in particular: an
  optional symbol's legitimately stale timestamp, e.g. a thin market,
  must never desynchronize the required BTC/ETH pair).
- verify_candidate_consistency() now takes an explicit symbol list; the
  original whole-decision-blocking check still runs against
  REQUIRED_SYMBOLS only, preserving prior behavior/reason strings exactly.
  A new per-symbol helper (candidate_consistency_errors_for_symbol) is
  reused to check each optional symbol independently in the main loop, so
  one optional symbol's inconsistent data can never block another's.
- Main aggregation loop iterates every symbol .13 reported (union with
  REQUIRED_SYMBOLS), splitting BLOCKED outcomes into required_blocked_count
  (still blocks the whole decision) vs. optional_symbols_blocked (recorded
  per-symbol, does not block).
- print_report() iterates actual decisions instead of a fixed BTC/ETH
  tuple, labeling each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL.

execution_permitted remains hard-coded False regardless of any of this.

Adds 11 contract tests, including a required-vs-optional timestamp-
desync test, an optional-symbol-inconsistency-blocks-only-that-symbol
test, and a cross-check that .13's mirror-candidate output still passes
.14's consistency contract unchanged. Also verified with a real .12-shaped
snapshot run through the actual .13 -> .14 chain (not just hand-built
fixtures): a BTC/ETH required pair plus a stale-timestamp AVAX mirror
candidate produces RISK_PASS with AVAX authorized independently and
execution_permitted still False. Full suite (32 tests) green.

